Development was organized into independent modules so that each could be built and tested separately. The authentication module manages registration, login, and sessions. The document selection module presents the available document types, and the question wizard builds its forms dynamically from JSON template definitions, so new documents can be added without rewriting the interface. For example, the NDA flow asks for the names of the parties, the nature of the confidential information, the duration of the agreement, the governing jurisdiction, and whether the agreement is one-way or mutual. The AI generation module combines the template with the user's answers into a prompt, calls the language model, and passes the result through a validation step that checks for missing clauses and inconsistencies. The explanation module then produces a plain-language note for each clause, and the editor module allows inline changes with version tracking. The export module produces PDF and DOCX files, and the dashboard module lists saved documents. Good engineering practices were followed throughout, including modular code, storing API keys in environment variables, sanitizing all input, handling errors gracefully, and committing regularly to a Git repository.
